
Finite-strain consistent tangent (stage 2 of the NLGEOM port).

Under NLGEOM the U3 element returns the exact derivative of the finite-strain
force, u3nltan.f, instead of the small-strain operator:

    du -> dF -> dF~ -> (dJ~, dJbar) -> dFbar -> dT -> dA -> df

with the ring weights at both ends, the cyclic chain inside dJbar, the Hencky
tangent in the eigenbasis of B = Fbar Fbar^T, and both terms of the
current-volume factor.  Rows are the ring and columns the support, so the deck
structure and the generator are untouched.  U2 is skipped under NLGEOM: the
finite-strain force already carries the deviatoric half.

VERIFIED: u3nltan matches FbarNL.tangent to 6e-15 at a finite field and the
small-strain operator to 5e-15 at u = 0 (tests/verify_nltan.py, which compiles
a per-edge driver); through CalculiX the corrections per increment are
quadratic (1.3e-2 -> 9.5e-4 -> 1.9e-6 -> 2.2e-11) and the reactions match the
prototype to 1.4e-7 (tests/verify_nlccx.py).

KNOWN LIMIT: at larger strain a trial state can invert an element; the element
returns a null block for that trial and ccx cuts the increment back, which
reaches roughly 1-2% strain on the MMS cell with the default step control.  A
line search or arc-length control on the ccx side is not part of this patch.

  Makefile.inc   builds u3nltan.f
  e_c3d_u.f      passes iperturb/vold to the U3 dispatcher
  mafillsmas.f   the same for the asymmetric assembly
  mafillsm.f     skips U2 under NLGEOM


